    "story": [
      "it is a top-down tree: a box is the parent of the boxes below it that a line joins it to, and access is inherited downward (said aloud); the lines have no arrowheads, so direction comes only from top and bottom",
      "Org: acme has two workspaces, Eng and Sales; Eng has Project: api and Project: web; api has Folder: secrets (restricted), which holds Doc: prod-db creds; web has Folder: design",
      "they moved Workspace: Sales up to line up with Workspace: Eng: same level of the tree",
      "the '...' under Workspace: Sales (two loose lines fanning down to it) is a collapsed subtree: they first drew Project: crm there, then erased it because Sales is the same shape as Eng and not relevant",
      "red is where the bug is (said aloud, no legend): the branch Workspace: Eng → Project: api → Folder: secrets (restricted) → Doc: prod-db creds",
      "the bug: an Eng member who is not on the security team can open Doc: prod-db creds",
      "the circle is around the doc itself, the thing that leaks; the underline is under '(restricted)'",
      "the red note beside the doc is their open question: does 'restricted' replace inherited roles or add to them; their other guess is that the doc checks the workspace role directly and skips the folder"
    ],
    "partner_should_ask_about": [
      "does a restricted folder replace inherited roles or add to them",
      "does the doc check its folder at all, or only the workspace role",
      "is there an org-level role (admin) that bypasses folder restrictions"
    ]
